      "markdown": "This app keeps your organisation's work in one place. After you sign in you land on\n**Home**, and everything else is one click away in the navigation on the left. This guide explains\neach part, and **Ask the Guide** answers questions about it in plain words.\n\n## How it is laid out\n\n- **Home** is where you start: shortcuts to the things you use most.\n- **The navigation** on the left groups the screens. What you see in it depends on your role: an\n  admin also sees **Settings** and **Activity**.\n- **The top bar** holds your notifications, your account menu and the **?** button.\n\n## Do it\n\n1. Open a screen from the navigation on the left.\n2. Press <kbd>?</kbd> on any screen (or click the **?** button in the top bar) to ask the guide a\n   question without leaving the page.\n3. Open **User guide** in the navigation to read it page by page, or search it from the box\n   above the contents.\n\n> **RULE OF THUMB** — Ask the Guide first when a screen is unfamiliar. Every answer links to the\n> page it came from, so you can read the whole story when you need it.\n\n## Watch out for\n\n- **A screen you expected is missing.** Your role decides what you can open. Ask an admin of your\n  organisation if you need more.\n- **The answer does not cover your question.** The guide only knows how the app works, not your\n  organisation's own data. Say what you were trying to do, and it will point you to the closest\n  page.\n",
